question:
What is printed by the following code?
int i = 2, s = 0;
switch (i) { case 1: s += 1; case 2: s += 2; case 3: s += 3; break; default: s += 5; }
printf("%d", s);

On a 64-bit machine, what does the following print?
void fun(int a[]) { printf("%zu", sizeof(a)); }
int main(void) { int arr[5]; fun(arr); return 0; }
